      "content": "I got a bit carried away with the goblin analogy. Here are the technical gates you'll typically want to consider for each stage:\n\n1. Code Commit:\n\t* Code review: Ensure that the code adheres to your organization's coding standards and best practices.\n\t* Static code analysis: Run tools like SonarQube or CodeCoverage to identify potential issues and areas for improvement.\n\t* Automated testing: Run unit tests and integration tests to ensure the code is working as expected.\n2. Automated Testing:\n\t* Unit testing: Ensure that individual units of code are working correctly.\n\t* Integration testing: Test how different components of the code interact with each other.\n\t* End-to-end testing: Test the entire application from start to finish.\n3. Staging:\n\t* Security scanning: Ensure that the code is free from known vulnerabilities.\n\t* Compliance scanning: Check for regulatory compliance with relevant standards (e.g. PCI-DSS, GDPR).\n\t* Performance testing: Test the application's performance under load to ensure it can handle expected traffic.\n4. Production:\n\t* Deployment validation: Verify that the code has been successfully deployed to production.\n\t* Monitoring and logging: Ensure that the application is properly monitored and logged for incident",
